parakeet-server for Debian
--------------------------

Models are not part of the package. Fetch the ones you want into
/var/lib/parakeet/models, the model directory compiled into this build:

    sudo parakeet-server --fetch tdt-0.6b-v2-q8_0.gguf
    sudo parakeet-server --fetch tdt-0.6b-v3-q8_0.gguf

Any file name from https://huggingface.co/mudler/parakeet-cpp-gguf works, as
do the aliases and URLs described in README.md in this directory.

Set the model to serve, the device and further options in
/etc/default/parakeet-server, then enable the service. It listens on
127.0.0.1:8081 by default:

    sudo systemctl enable --now parakeet-server

A request may select any other fetched model by file name:

    curl -F file=@audio.wav -F model=tdt-0.6b-v3-q8_0.gguf \
        http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/audio/transcriptions

The service runs as a dynamic user in the render and video groups, so
PARAKEET_DEVICE=Vulkan0 in /etc/default/parakeet-server can use the GPU.

 -- Ronny Rentner <debian@ronny-rentner.de>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0100
